//! Config writers — one module per target.
//!
//! # To add a new target:
//!
//!   1. Create `src/writers/my_app.rs`
//!   2. `pub struct MyApp;`
//!   3. `impl Writer for MyApp { ... }`
//!   4. `mod my_app; pub use my_app::MyApp;` here in mod.rs
//!   5. Add `Box::new(MyApp)` to `all_writers()` below.
//!
//! # Writer contract:
//!
//! - Writers NEVER touch the user's own config files. Each writer owns one
//!   generated file and writes it wholesale on every theme switch.
//! - The user imports that file from their own config (include, require,
//!   @import, dofile, ...). No exceptions for formats without an import
//!   mechanism: there the generated file is a snippet the user merges once,
//!   and the header says exactly that.
//! - Every generated file starts with a header comment: "Generated by
//!   theme-manager" plus a "To use:" tutorial with the exact import line.
//!
//! Wallpaper processes are managed by [`crate::wallpaper`], not by writers.

